@okwasniewski, can you confirm that e2e should reject `test.skip()` and `test.fixme()` with `INVALID_ARGUMENT` when they’re called from `afterEach` or fixture teardown after a test that did not already skip? I’d keep the refusal, consistent with late `test.fail()`.

@Asheesh7298, could you also update the [Throws row](https://github.com/e2e-inc/e2e/blob/6e857486625e871bfb879ed836b6222aa21c8f95/docs/reference/test.mdx#L134) and its Japanese and Chinese mirrors? I checked Playwright 1.65.1. A late skip preserves the original failure and adds no cleanup error, but it still changes the expected status to `skipped`. That makes a failure marked with `test.fail()` unexpected, so “ignores the call after a failure” is too broad.
